    "b-40-prompt-system-prompt-kit-is-a-sibling-6": {
      "id": "b-40-prompt-system-prompt-kit-is-a-sibling-6",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 3
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Prompt-kit is a sibling repo, not a kernel package"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-prompt-system-decision-the-generi-7": {
      "id": "b-40-prompt-system-decision-the-generi-7",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decision:",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " The generic prompt document model (AST, canonicalization and\nhashing, renderers, transforms, validation) lives in\n"
        },
        {
          "insert": "@codecaine-ai/prompt-kit",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", in the Core workspace's "
        },
        {
          "insert": "prompt-kit",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " repo\n("
        },
        {
          "insert": "prompt-kit/packages/prompt-kit",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "). The kernel consumes it and its companion "
        },
        {
          "insert": "@codecaine-ai/prompt-kit-server",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " as workspace dependencies. The edit-op compiler lives in "
        },
        {
          "insert": "@codecaine-ai/prompt-kit/authoring",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " and is shared with the Prompt MCP. "
        },
        {
          "insert": "prompt-edit-session/compile-ops.ts",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " re-exports it. Kernel-specific prompt helpers exist only in the kernel, and\nonly when they truly depend on kernel concepts."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-prompt-system-why-the-original-pl-8": {
      "id": "b-40-prompt-system-why-the-original-pl-8",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Why:",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " The original plan kept prompt-kit at "
        },
        {
          "insert": "packages/prompt-kit",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " inside\nthis repo. That coupled a generic, reusable prompt standard to kernel\nreleases and kernel tooling; the peer repo lets other harnesses consume it\nwithout pulling the kernel workspace. The dependency direction is the design\ninvariant either way: kernel → prompt-kit, never the reverse."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-prompt-system-applies-to-any-new-9": {
      "id": "b-40-prompt-system-applies-to-any-new-9",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Applies to:",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " Any new prompt AST node, renderer, transform, or edit operation:\nit goes to the "
        },
        {
          "insert": "prompt-kit",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " repo, not "
        },
        {
          "insert": "packages/kernel",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". Any new kernel code\nimporting prompt-kit does so through the package export, never a relative\npath."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-prompt-system-prompt-writes-shared-store-38": {
      "id": "b-40-prompt-system-prompt-writes-shared-store-38",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 3
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Prompt writes go through the shared prompt store"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-prompt-system-decision-shared-store-39": {
      "id": "b-40-prompt-system-decision-shared-store-39",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decision:",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " "
        },
        {
          "insert": "savePrompt",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " in "
        },
        {
          "insert": "catalog-service.ts",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " writes through "
        },
        {
          "insert": "createPromptStore",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " from "
        },
        {
          "insert": "@codecaine-ai/prompt-kit-server",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", the same store the Prompt MCP uses. The kernel and the MCP share one per-file lock, one journal, and one "
        },
        {
          "insert": "expectedHash",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " compare-and-swap base. When disk-sync finds an MCP edit through the store journal ("
        },
        {
          "insert": "readLatestPromptChange",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "), it records the revision with source "
        },
        {
          "insert": "prompt-kit-mcp",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-prompt-system-why-shared-store-40": {
      "id": "b-40-prompt-system-why-shared-store-40",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Why:",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " Two writers with separate locks could interleave on one "
        },
        {
          "insert": "prompt.json",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " and lose an edit. One store gives one conflict rule, a 409 with "
        },
        {
          "insert": "{ currentHash }",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " for whichever writer is stale, and one revision history that includes MCP edits."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-prompt-system-applies-shared-store-41": {
      "id": "b-40-prompt-system-applies-shared-store-41",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Applies to:",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " Any new code path that writes "
        },
        {
          "insert": "prompt.json",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". It calls the shared store and never writes the file directly."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-prompt-system-bundle-sections-resolve-10": {
      "id": "b-40-prompt-system-bundle-sections-resolve-10",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 3
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Bundle sections resolve by filename convention, file-first"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-prompt-system-decision-bundle-res-11": {
      "id": "b-40-prompt-system-decision-bundle-res-11",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decision:",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " Bundle resolution is one module:\n"
        },
        {
          "insert": "agent-registry/registry/bundle-layout.ts",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". Every section follows the\n"
        },
        {
          "insert": "<kind>.ts | <kind>/index.ts",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " rule ("
        },
        {
          "insert": "prompt.json | prompt/prompt.json",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " for\nthe prompt); the file form is tried first and wins silently when both exist,\nwith the shadowed path recorded for "
        },
        {
          "insert": "doctor --catalog",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". "
        },
        {
          "insert": "index.ts",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " is a\nfolder's only entry point; everything else in a section folder is invisible\nto discovery."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-prompt-system-why-the-rejected-al-12": {
      "id": "b-40-prompt-system-why-the-rejected-al-12",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Why:",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " The rejected alternative was pointing at section files from\n"
        },
        {
          "insert": "agent.json",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". Path fields would make the manifest a build config instead of\ndata, and every migration would need a manifest edit; the convention keeps\nmanifests schema-validated data and makes re-export shims safe mid-move."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-prompt-system-applies-to-any-new-13": {
      "id": "b-40-prompt-system-applies-to-any-new-13",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Applies to:",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " Any new bundle section or sidecar kind: extend\n"
        },
        {
          "insert": "bundle-layout.ts",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " and follow the same two legal shapes. No other code may\nprobe bundle directories directly."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-prompt-system-manifest-and-sidecar-con-14": {
      "id": "b-40-prompt-system-manifest-and-sidecar-con-14",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 3
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Manifest and sidecar contracts live in "
