        {
          "insert": "agent-definition/",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-prompt-system-decision-packages-15": {
      "id": "b-40-prompt-system-decision-packages-15",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decision:",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " "
        },
        {
          "insert": "packages/kernel/src/agent-definition/",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " owns the\n"
        },
        {
          "insert": "agent-kernel/agent-v1",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " JSON Schema ("
        },
        {
          "insert": "agent-manifest-schema.ts",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "), the\n"
        },
        {
          "insert": "defineAgent",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " generator/validator, and "
        },
        {
          "insert": "defineSpawnerTool",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". The registry\nvalidates every "
        },
        {
          "insert": "agent.json",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " against this one schema; no other module\ndefines manifest fields."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-prompt-system-why-the-alternative-16": {
      "id": "b-40-prompt-system-why-the-alternative-16",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Why:",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " The alternative, letting the registry, spawn pipeline, and viewer\neach carry their own notion of manifest fields, is how the retired\nfrontmatter model drifted. One schema module means a new manifest field is\nadded exactly once and every consumer sees it through the parsed\n"
        },
        {
          "insert": "ParsedAgent.config",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-prompt-system-applies-to-any-new-17": {
      "id": "b-40-prompt-system-applies-to-any-new-17",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Applies to:",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " Any new manifest field, sidecar declaration shape, or\nvariable-schema rule: schema first, in "
        },
        {
          "insert": "agent-definition/",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", then consumers."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-prompt-system-the-state-model-is-one-k-18": {
      "id": "b-40-prompt-system-the-state-model-is-one-k-18",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 3
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The state model is one kernel module behind one gate"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-prompt-system-decision-everything-19": {
      "id": "b-40-prompt-system-decision-everything-19",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decision:",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " Everything the state model ships (the extension, the\nthree-section builder, window policies, the context set, the snapshot store,\nand the kernel-side message helpers) lives in "
        },
        {
          "insert": "packages/kernel/src/state/",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ".\nRegistration is gated on "
        },
        {
          "insert": "stateExtensionEnabled",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " (a "
        },
        {
          "insert": "state.ts",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " sidecar or a\n"
        },
        {
          "insert": "state.window",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " manifest block); with neither, nothing is registered."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-prompt-system-why-the-rejected-sh-20": {
      "id": "b-40-prompt-system-why-the-rejected-sh-20",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Why:",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " The rejected shape was always registering the extension with no-op\nbehavior for plain agents. Mechanical absence is what makes the pass-through\nguarantee (design D83) auditable: a byte-identical legacy session cannot be\npromised by a code path that still runs."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
